[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4268413955","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118678#issuecomment-4268413955","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118678","id":4268413955,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7-atQD","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-17T13:35:24Z","updated_at":"2026-04-17T13:59:37Z","body":"I would like to amend this a little bit in the sense that I believe this is the only way to resolve this problem *without changing semantics of `unreference()`* \r\n\r\nRight now both the `rc_val == 0` and `rc_val == 1` cases have observable effects outside of the class. In some cases GDExtension callbacks are called.\r\n\r\nThere's ways of achieving clean shutdown without this refcount, mostly by moving more of the cleanup code to `Object::~Object()` but this would have API observable changes.\r\n\r\nI think we *should* do this for Godot 5. But I don't see a way of retaining the api contract otherwise.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4268413955/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4295320788","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118678#issuecomment-4295320788","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118678","id":4295320788,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABAAVk1A","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-22T10:06:35Z","updated_at":"2026-04-22T10:06:35Z","body":"> Makes sense crash wise, but note that this introduces a pretty significant cost to `RefCounted`, both size wise and performance wise.\r\n> \r\n> I'm not sure what's prompting the current code to notify extensions and scripts to decrement also on one instead of just 0, but changing to notify on just 0 would also fix the issue.\r\n\r\nI totally agree, but that would change the API contract so I didn't want to do it. If we can figure out why we notify on both we should change it. But there very well might be GDExtensions that rely on this behavior.","author_association"